#lego-legacy-route 1
# LEGO Chess, from its boot into its throne room and out: Space skips Krisalis' logo and the intro,
# a new player is made at the New Player form with no name typed, and the window is closed (#210).
#
# Replay it with a fresh `--data-root <empty dir>`, never beside the rip. It reaches the New Player
# form only when no profile is saved, and it saves one: the game writes profiles\prof1.lcp and
# profiles\1save.lcs for the player it makes, which beside the rip would land among the live saves
# in game-data/chess/profile, and the next replay would boot past the form.
#
# The logo plays through, and Space skips Krisalis' logo as in skip-krisalis.route: down at flip
# 290 and up at the 300th poll after it, and the intro opens after flip 294. Space goes down again
# at flip 300, as the intro plays: the game ends it, waits for Space to come up (0x0040D220),
# presenting nothing, and Space comes up at the 300th poll after the flip. The movie player clears
# the screen twice, flips 301 and 302, and the game draws its bumper through Direct3D 2, flips 303 and
# 304. While the bumper stands it loads its rooms' files and decodes their first fifteen sounds
# (#153), going on without the one neither pressing ships, sounds\YAHOO.wav; flip 305 is black.
# With no profile saved it asks for a new player: flip 306 has the form's buttons and boxes on
# black, and from flip 307 the New Player form stands on parchment between the inkpot and the
# quill, its name box's caret first on at flip 319.
#
# The pointer goes to the tick at flip 320, and the left button goes down at flip 330: the game
# waits for it to come up, presenting nothing, which it does at the 300th poll after the flip. With
# no name typed the game names the player LEGO® Chess 1, saves it, and lists it under "Who's
# playing?". The tick, pressed again at flip 370 and let go at its 300th poll, takes the only player
# in: the game decodes twelve more sounds, and the throne room presents from flip 372, the camera
# flying in to the King by flip 380 as he starts speaking, heard from flip 374. The window is closed
# at flip 400, and the game leaves.
flip 290 key Space down
flip 290 poll 300 key Space up
flip 300 key Space down
flip 300 poll 300 key Space up
flip 320 move 576 420
flip 330 down
flip 330 poll 300 up
flip 370 down
flip 370 poll 300 up
flip 400 close
